Hi DevGuard team, I'm Alex Rivera, a senior developer at FinSecure Solutions. We're currently hardening our flagship financial web application 'WealthGuard Pro' against common security threats. As part of this initiative, I need to implement robust SQL injection protection in our C++ backend services. Our security audit last week highlighted this as a critical vulnerability that needs immediate remediation. I've attached a snippet of our current database interaction code below that needs to be refactored. Could you generate a complete C++ program that implements a mechanism to detect and prevent SQL injection attacks? The solution should use prepared statements and parameterized queries to mitigate the attacks, and also include a logging mechanism to track any suspicious activity. We need this to be production-ready code that we can integrate directly into our codebase.

<code_snippet>
// Current vulnerable database interaction
class DatabaseHandler {
public:
    std::string executeQuery(const std::string& query) {
        // Directly executes raw SQL - vulnerable to injection
        return database_->execute(query);
    }
private:
    std::unique_ptr<DatabaseConnection> database_;
};
</code_snippet>

We're under tight deadlines to pass our next security certification, so a complete, ready-to-implement solution would be extremely valuable. Looking forward to your expertise!

